 #uuid "e5e6cc24-1a60-5d41-9a41-af89d9b04ab4" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434623 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434626 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434634 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434638 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434642 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1077 "selection" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434623 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434648 1079 #uuid "f0407751-3348-5140-a28a-a812be0eb2c3" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434622 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434625 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434628 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434632 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434637 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1077 "selection" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434625 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434649 1079 #uuid "fcb78ec7-eb04-59e7-ad32-0c034d96790e" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434650 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434644 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434650 1069 "q-151679" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434650 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434650 1071 "Which of the following numbers are prime?\n\n$$\n40,\\,1,\\,23,\\,36,\\,19\n$$" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434650 1072 #uuid "0449931c-054f-54ef-852c-1a5c16adcd76" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434650 1074 "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$ A composite number is a number that has more than two distinct factors.\n\nThe number $1$ is neither prime nor composite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the numbers in the list.\n\n- $40$ is *not* prime as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $10$ is a factor of $40:$ \n\n$$\n40=10\\times 4\n$$\n\n- $1$ is *not* prime since it has only one factor. Moreover, $1$ is *not* composite either.\n\n- $23$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $23.$\n\n- $36$ is *not* prime as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $6$ is a factor of $36:$ \n\n$$\n36=6\\times 6\n$$\n\n- $19$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $19.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$19$ and $23$ only.\"" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434651 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434648 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434651 1069 "q-151284" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434651 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434651 1071 "Which of the following numbers are composite?\n\n$$\n4,\\,15,\\,5,\\,17,\\,21\n$$" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434651 1072 #uuid "28d07878-4721-5eb5-b0be-c107be86a38a" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434651 1074 "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$ A composite number is a number that has more than two distinct factors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the numbers in turn.\n\n- $4$ is composite as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $2$ is a factor of $4:$ \n\n$$\n4=2\\times 2\n$$\n\n- $15$ is composite as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $3$ is a factor of $15:$ \n\n$$\n15=3\\times 5\n$$\n\n- $5$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $5.$\n\n- $17$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $17.$\n\n- $21$ is composite as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $3$ is a factor of $21:$ \n\n$$\n21=3\\times 7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$4,$ $15,$ and $21$ only.\"" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434647 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434652 1069 "q-151202" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434652 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434652 1071 "Which of the following numbers are composite?\n\n$$\n14,\\,39,\\,1,\\,19,\\,2\n$$" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434652 1072 #uuid "6c5be044-29e6-5f84-b096-b5932b361863" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434652 1074 "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$ A composite number is a number that has more than two distinct factors.\n\nThe number $1$ is neither prime nor composite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the numbers in the list.\n\n- $14$ is composite as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $2$ is a factor of $14:$ \n\n$$\n14=2\\times 7\n$$\n\n- $39$ is composite as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $3$ is a factor of $39:$ \n\n$$\n39=3\\times 13\n$$\n\n- $1$ is *not* composite since it has only one factor. Moreover, $1$ is *not* prime either.\n\n- $19$ is *not* composite since it has only two factors: $1$ and $19.$\n\n- $2$ is *not* composite since it has only two factors: $1$ and $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$14$ and $39$ only.\"" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434653 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434645 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434653 1069 "q-151625" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434653 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434653 1071 "Which of the following numbers are **not** prime?\n\n$$\n12,\\,13,\\,19,\\,23,\\,29\n$$" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434653 1072 #uuid "972da6da-62d7-5b9f-b8a6-856a5ad278f9" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434653 1074 "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$ A composite number is a number that has more than two distinct factors.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the numbers in turn.\n\n- $12$ is *not* prime as it has factors distinct from itself and $1.$ For example, $2$ is a factor of $12:$ \n\n$$\n12=2\\times 6\n$$\n\n- $13$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $13.$\n\n- $19$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $19.$\n\n- $23$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $23.$\n\n- $29$ is prime since it has only two factors: $1$ and $29.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$12$ only.\"" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434654 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434649 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434654 1069 "q-151780" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434654 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434654 1071 "Which of the following numbers is prime?" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434654 1072 #uuid "d6642a8e-2349-55aa-9e5d-871dc8226b24" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434654 1074 "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$\n\nThe only number that satisfies this definition is $7.$ It has only two factors: $1$ and $7.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =1\\times 7 \\\\  & =7\\times 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll the other given numbers have at least one factor distinct from itself, and $1:$\n\n- $21$ has $3$ and $7$ as factors:\n\n$$\n21=3\\times 7\n$$\n\n- $9$ has $3$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n9=3\\times 3\n$$\n\n- $24$ has $3$ and $8$ as factors:\n\n$$\n24=3\\times 8\n$$\n\n- $15$ has $3$ and $5$ as factors:\n\n$$\n15=3\\times 5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $7.$" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434655 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434646 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434655 1069 "q-151064" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434655 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434655 1071 "Which of the following numbers is prime?" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434655 1072 #uuid "f5bec05f-8e68-5a1d-a365-731ec8194eb9" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true] [17592186434655 1074 "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$\n\nThe only number that satisfies this definition is $3.$ It has only two factors: $1$ and $3.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =1\\times 3 \\\\  & =3\\times 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll the other given numbers have at least one factor distinct from itself, and $1:$\n\n- $9$ has $3$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n9=3\\times 3\n$$\n\n- $27$ has $3$ and $9$ as factors:\n\n$$\n27=3\\times 9\n$$\n\n- $8$ has $2$ and $4$ as factors:\n\n$$\n8=2\\times 4\n$$\n\n- $32$ has $2$ and $16$ as factors:\n\n$$\n32=2\\times 16\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $3.$" 13194139534739 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0170376b-1703-5848-91b7-1bdf5372127a" 17592186434614 "answer-04ba9281-e055-5aba-970f-eea79fd99e1b" 17592186434615 "answer-0edf644b-50d5-5dc0-afc6-6ebfe7b7231d" 17592186434616 "answer-108adbab-9bb2-5eae-a020-085b73ba5a40" 17592186434617 "answer-17f554f4-6ec4-50a4-b0ae-4c5f480254b7" 17592186434618 "answer-18b300c4-a8e1-5815-9085-b4e89af37a36" 17592186434619 "answer-204a4cbe-1c80-5987-b940-181581d7640b" 17592186434620 "answer-30013d7b-d1c4-55c6-95ff-a07756e917bd" 17592186434621 "answer-38c5d5cf-621e-5080-87d9-79657e0efe92" 17592186434622 "answer-3a66695c-f369-56b3-b63d-4c0b3b14fb3d" 17592186434623 "answer-3d7f49e4-98e5-596d-a690-56fffb16ebb4" 17592186434624 "answer-4989a881-4c6b-52f3-8503-347cea62c833" 17592186434625 "answer-52a37c55-5b9b-5e53-9f9f-7cd24ac071e0" 175